      "writtenOn": "2022-08-02T15:13:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For sure clang-format and our style guide don\u0027t always 100% agree. For instance the style guide asks for \"one initializer per line\" but in practice, clang-format will pack them all on one line if they fit. (It will do one-per-line if they don\u0027t fit though.) \n\nWe should probably try to get these two things in closer alignment. clang-format has a lot of knobs we can tweak. And of course we can always update the guide in places where it\u0027s out of date or where clang-format can\u0027t be made to do what we want it to.",
